schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-creature-the-unmade
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of the Unmade — an ambient entity found in Zone 8,
    the Threshold. This creature is rendered in strictly black and white and is barely
    visible — an entity of pure void, the place where light goes to die. The Unmade has
    no fixed form — it is a negative space in the world, a region where reality simply
    stops existing. The viewer perceives it primarily by what it is not: the background
    continues on either side of the creature but is absent where the creature exists, as
    if something has been erased from the image. There is a sense of wrongness in
    perceiving it — the brain tries to fill in what should be there and fails. Edges of
    the erased region shimmer slightly, as if the boundary between existence and
    non-existence is turbulent. Where the Unmade moves, the ground beneath is simply
    gone — not destroyed but never-was. The composition should feel like looking at a
    photograph with a section carefully cut out, except the cut-out section is moving
    toward the viewer. No eyes, no mouth, no limbs — the horror is in the absence of
    anything to relate to. The background is the Threshold's black and white void with
    floating architectural fragments. Painterly style, but the Unmade itself is rendered
    as absence of paint, of detail, of existence. The mood is existential negation.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, any color, visible creature, ghost, wraith, shadow figure, cloaked figure, eyes, face, limbs, colorful palette, low detail, flat shading, solid black shape, solid white shape"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1024
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "2:3"

tags: [creature, ambient-enemy, zone-8, void, unmade, absence, concept-art, dark-fantasy, black-and-white]
